{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/922509-enneagram-and-families","id":922509,"title":"Enneagram and Families","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-28T01:59:57-07:00","id":922509,"title":"Enneagram and Families","content":"so, I've stumbled upon <a href=\"http://characterchange.com/9-fundamental-fears-that-motivate-your-characters/\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> and I've immediately thought about Beast. In sort, this is another &quot;personality diagram&quot; which express 9 &quot;basic Fears&quot; among others, and I've thought how would Beast's Families may work in that diagram or what new potential Families one could make from those ideas. Anakim seems to be the &quot;Fear of Worthlessness&quot; (you are no more than dust before the living mountain), Makara connects to the &quot;Fear of Lacking Support&quot; (one wrong step and you fall into the depths), Eshmaki may be the &quot;Fear of Loss&quot; (darkness creeps through the little cracks), Namtaru are probably the &quot;Fear being Unloved&quot; (even you can't look at yourself in the mirror) and the Ugallu are the most likely the &quot;Fear of Insignificance&quot; (all look the same from up in the sky, and all are as vulnerable no matter who you are or what you do). The character types themselves could be used as Hero inspiration based around those fears. That also leaves 4 more types of Fears as potential Families- Fear of Corruption, Incompetence, Deprivation and Control.<br /> <br /> So- what do you think? What would Beasts may think on such categorization? Does it really has potential for new Families or something?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T06:02:08-07:00","id":922565,"title":"","content":"Huh. I am definitely curious to see what sort of Families could be conceptualized from those four Fears.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T07:00:06-07:00","id":922592,"title":"","content":"When I think of &quot;fear of being controlled,&quot; I think of dreams where you are trapped or restrained. Nightmares where you are running as hard as you can, but you are moving at a crawl. Spiders, squid, anything that can wrap you up, who slowly descend upon you or pull you closer to your inevitable doom. <br /> <br /> No ideas for any of the other three. I can certainly think of Nightmares that would invoke those fears, but I can't think of concepts of families that are sufficiently unique that I don't end up thinking &quot;They're like X family, but...&quot; or &quot;They're like a cross between X family and Y family.&quot; Also, I'm not familiar enough with ancient Mesopotamian mythology to take a stab at trying to name any new families.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T00:13:39-07:00","id":923120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/922509-enneagram-and-families?p=922592#post922592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I think of &quot;fear of being controlled,&quot; I think of dreams where you are trapped or restrained. Nightmares where you are running as hard as you can, but you are moving at a crawl. Spiders, squid, anything that can wrap you up, who slowly descend upon you or pull you closer to your inevitable doom.</div> </div> </div> </div>yeah, that's also what I've had in mind, with adding some elements of &quot;fear your own fate&quot; to it. That kind of Fear is kinda obvious, and if I'll decide to write a Family from that list it would be that one. As for the others, while on the surface they are similar to the other 5 Families they could be interpreted in a quit different direction- Fear of Corruption, for example, is Fear of becoming &quot;evil&quot;. It is the kind of fear which triggered witch hunts and inquisitions of all kinds, what that makes people &quot;purify&quot; themselves constantly and hate themselves for not being &quot;good enough&quot;. Succubi and their kind feel like a good manifestation of that kind of Fear.<br /> <br /> Fear of Incompetence, from what I can see, is not meant to be a fear from lacking power as much as it is a fear about lacking knowledge- it is a fear from not being able to act, not being talented or skilled enough to deal with a problem. It is you forgetting your pants before a big lecture- it is a stage fright, a moment before the show is on and your tongue getting stuck in your mouth. It is you being mocked, you being unable to save yourself. While it may share a few elements with the Makara (like, you don't know how to swim), with the later there is something hungry bellow you which tries to drag you to the depth. In the first you drown because of your own lackings, and you are doomed because you simply weren't good enough. Still no idea for what kind of monster it could be represented as.<br /> <br /> As for Fear of Deprivation, on the surface it does feels connected to Fear of Loss, which is related to the Eshmaki- but it is more personal. Is not about being abandoned and alone in the dark, or having all you care about turned into ash. It is about lacking things which are essential to your existence- you are lost in the desert, with no oasis at sight. You are in the middle of the wilderness, forced into losing your own humanity in order to survive. It is about a need so strong which can not be fulfilled, about yearning toward nothing more than a cup of water or a warm embrace in the middle of the snow. All kinds of vampiric monsters may be related to that concept, I think.<br /> <br /> Also, just to not- while Middle Eastern terminology does seem to be the theme for Family names, Mesopotamian in not the only one- sure, Namatru and Ugallu are, but Anakim is a biblical term- which mean, it comes from the Levant, which is close but still different, and Eshmaki is (as far as I can tell) a Georgian term, which is even more fur away, while Makara comes from India. In sort, there is not need to limit yourself for Mesopotamian names for Families when even the book doesn't do so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}